   [KB-Image "AVL Tree Double Left Rotation"]

- **Right-Right (Double Right) Rotation**: Similar to the left-left rotation, we first perform a left rotation on the node's grandchild and then a right rotation on the node. This is also known as a double right rotation.

   [KB-Image "AVL Tree Double Right Rotation"]

- **Left-Right (Right-Left) Rotations**: These are a combination of a left rotation on the parent of the original grandchild and a right rotation on the grandchild itself. They help in maintaining balance when the height difference between the two subtrees of the root exceeds 2, with the left subtree being taller.

   [KB-Image "AVL Tree Left-Right Rotation"]

- **Right-Left (Left-Right) Rotations**: These are a combination of a right rotation on the parent of the original grandchild and a left rotation on the grandchild itself. They help in maintaining balance when the height difference between the two subtrees of the root exceeds 2, with the right subtree being taller.

   [KB-Image "AVL Tree Right-Left Rotation"]

