In an AVL tree, each node has a balance factor that represents the difference between the heights of the left and right subtrees. The balance factor is calculated as follows:

Balance Factor (BF) = Height(Left Subtree) - Height(Right Subtree)

The rules for an AVL tree are:
1. BF of any node must be between -1 and 1.
2. A new node has a balance factor of 0.
3. Rotations are performed to maintain the above conditions.

