    / \
   3   9
   ```  
   After Right Rotation (RR):
   ```
   / \
  3   9
    / \
   7   5
   ```

3. **Two-Child Left Rotation (2CLR)**:** This rotation is needed when a right subtree has two children, and LR would not balance the tree.

   ```markdown
   Original AVL Tree:
   ```
   / \
  5   9
    / \
   7   11
   ```  
   After Two-Child Left Rotation (2CLR):
   ```
   / \
  3   9
    / \
   7   11
     / \
    5   10
   ```

In summary, AVL tree rotations are performed to maintain the balance property of an AVL tree. Depending on the type of imbalance, one or more rotation operations may be necessary.
