   - Instead of moving the right child up, we move the left child down to become the new root (`w`).
   - Then, we reassign `x`'s left and right children. `x.left = w` and `x.right = y`.
   - The result is that the height of the right subtree of `y` has decreased by one.

Both rotations are performed to maintain the AVL property, which ensures that the difference in heights between the left and right subtrees of any node never exceeds one.
